error[NK1335]: `P::pick` hands back a view of `b`'s data, but its result says `from a`.
   --> tests/an_impl_handing_back_an_owned_parameter_is_refused_once.nika:36:5
    |
 36 |     fn pick(self, a: String, b: String) -> String from a {
    |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    |
    = note: A caller reads the signature: it keeps `a` unchanged while the result is used, and nothing holds `b` (ADR-views-3 D8).
    = help: Write `from a | b`, or hand back a copy of what comes from `b` with `.clone()`.
